.TH CAT 1
.SH NAME
cat \- show files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cat
.IR file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cat
is a command built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
It writes each
.I file
to the terminal, one after the other, as it is. A file that cannot be read
is named with the reason, and
.B cat
goes on with the next.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 if a file could not be read.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR echo (1),
.BR ls (1),
.BR man (1)
.SH BUGS
It reads only files: there is no standard input to copy.
